Perfect! I have all the details. Let me compile your findings with the code locations and the bug analysis:

## 1. **Theme Mode Switching Logic** — ⚠️ **FOUND THE BUG**

**File:** [packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl#L270-L415)

**Bug Location:** Lines 398-410

**The Problem:**
The "Appearance" mode picker hardcodes "system" as initially selected but **never runs the theme calculation on page load**:

```typescript
// Line 398: Always marks "system" as selected without calculating the actual mode
if (appearance === "system") option.classList.add("is-selected");

// Lines 400-410: The click handler that *should* run on load, but doesn't
option.addEventListener("click", () => {
  const selectedMode =
    appearance === "system"
      ? window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches  // ← Never evaluated at load
        ? "dark"
        : "light"
      : appearance;
  document.body.dataset.appearanceMode = appearance;
  document.documentElement.style.colorScheme = selectedMode;
  document.documentElement.dataset.pantokenScheme = selectedMode;
  // ... applies chrome theme, editor theme
});
```

**Why the bug happens:**
- User's OS is dark → page loads
- "system" option is marked `.is-selected` via CSS
- But the click handler is **never triggered**, so `matchMedia("prefers-color-scheme: dark")` is never called
- DOM attributes (`data-pantoken-scheme`, `colorScheme`) are never set based on OS preference
- Result: UI shows "system" selected, but rendering uses uninitialized/default (light) theme
- **When user clicks "light" then back to "system":** the click handler fires, `matchMedia()` runs correctly, and dark theme applies

**Root Cause:** Missing initialization of system theme on page load. The shell setup function should calculate and apply the system mode before returning.

---

## 2. **Color/Theme Picker** — Swatches + Selection Indicator

**File:** [packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/app.html](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/app.html#L194-L335)  
**CSS:** [packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/app.css](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/app.css#L286-L340)  
**JS Logic:** [main.ts.tmpl](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl#L416-L425)

**Color Options (13 total):**
Rendered in a grid with data-driven color swatches:
- `navy`, `blue`, `green`, `red`, `orange`, `grey`, `plum`, `violet`, `stone`, `sky`, `honey`, `sea`, `aurora`

**Selection Indicator:**
Each color option is a button with:
```html
<button class="canvas-rce-shell__option" data-color="navy">
  <span class="theme-picker__swatch" data-swatch="navy"></span>
  <span>Navy</span>
  <span class="canvas-rce-shell__mark"><!-- Check icon --></span>
</button>
```

**CSS Classes:**
- `.canvas-rce-shell__option` — base button, padding `0.5rem 0.625rem`, flex centered
- `.canvas-rce-shell__option.is-selected` — border + background applied via `.is-selected` class toggle
- `.theme-picker__swatch` — `1rem × 1rem` circular swatch with background color from CSS variables
  - `var(--instui-primitive-color-{color}-{color}70)` (e.g., `--instui-primitive-color-navy-navy70`)
  - Box shadow: `inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,0.15)`
- `.canvas-rce-shell__mark` — contains a lucide `Check` icon, opacity 0 by default, shown on `.is-selected`

**JS Selection:** [Lines 424-428](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl#L424-L428)
```typescript
option.addEventListener("click", () => {
  if (isThemeColor(color)) {
    applyChromeColor(color);  // Sets data-pantoken-color
    document.documentElement.dataset.pantokenColor = color;
  }
  // Toggle .is-selected on all color buttons
  for (const candidate of themePanel.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-color]")) {
    candidate.classList.toggle("is-selected", candidate.dataset.color === color);
  }
});
```

